Z||000000||Shaun41178||07-27-2001||12:16 AM||||i made a video of a few races and I would like to post them on the internet for others to download.  however I don't know how to do this.  I am guessing you need a program or something?<P>I recorded the race on a mini vhs tape.  Anyone know how to upload this tape?  I would appreciate any help.  like a total walk through as I am not too proficient at this kind of stuff  Thanks!!!<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds||||reg||5
Z||000001||Songman||07-27-2001||12:25 AM||||First, you'll have to convert it to some internet-compatible file format.. Then you'll have to have enough web space somewhere to store it. And then you'll have to have an FTP program or something like that to upload it, unless the place you are storing it has web uploading...<P>Some of the available formats for the web are mpgand avi. There are others of course...<P>I can't tell you any free place that will offer enough space to store videos. They are generally pretty large in size.<P>CuteFTP is what I use to upload to my sites. Well, it used to be anyway. Now I mostly upload with the ftp program built into GoLive.<P>Good luck.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shaun41178||07-27-2001||12:34 AM||||thanks songman for the quick reply.  I knew that I had to convert the tape to a mpg format as that is how I want to do it but dont' know what kind of program I need or where to get it or even how to hook up the tape recorder to the computer to get it on my hard drive.  Thats what I need help with at first<P>i am guessing someone might have some extra space here to put it on their site for like 2 weeks or so.  thats all Ineed it up for.  <P>I just want to get it onto my computer and in a different format first and then take it from there.  Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||07-27-2001||12:47 AM||||I have an intel PC camera, with a little video in outlet on the back.  It says in the book I can hook up a video line right from my camcorder to the back of the Intel camera and directly transfer video.  Seems easy enough.  I got it brand new for round 65 bucks on ebay.  You can probably get a program to convert on <A HREF="http://www.downloads.com" TARGET=_blank>www.downloads.com</A> ||||reg||1
